invariant: INV-14
file: srv_message.h
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: a QUIC server stages its EncryptedExtensions in a frame with no room
  for the transport parameters RFC 9001 section 8.2 makes it send, so
  srv_build_encrypted_extensions returns 0 and the handshake fails with
  CH_ECAP after the ServerHello once the body passes about 45 bytes.
  bin/srv_quic_test runs its flight with the largest body the API admits
  and builds the largest message at the frame's size exactly.

--- old
#define SRV_ENCRYPTED_EXTENSIONS_MAX (6 + 7 + CH_ALPN_NAME_MAX + 4 + CH_TRANSPORT_PARAMS_MAX)
--- new
#define SRV_ENCRYPTED_EXTENSIONS_MAX (6 + 7 + CH_ALPN_NAME_MAX)
